# Shared Phoenixcoin mainnet chain fragment for the LMDB regression scripts.
#
# These are real mainnet blocks 1-4, exactly as returned by getblock <hash> 0.
# They are used instead of mined blocks because block 1 is a hardened
# checkpoint: a synthetic block cannot be connected without weakening
# consensus checks, and solving the 2^20-difficulty scrypt proof of work once
# per test run would make the tests impractically slow.  The blocks are
# submitted through the normal submitblock -> ProcessBlock path, so they still
# exercise real block validation and connection code.
#
# Source this file from bash; it only defines variables.

